"""Hand-written English method descriptions, part 5: equipment Cable and Bands.

Keyed by the v5 catalog slug (slugify of the canonical exercise name).
Merged by build_progression.py as the last description tier; a key that
matches no catalog row fails the build, so typos surface immediately.
"""

DESCRIPTIONS = {
    "banded_adductor_stretch": "The banded adductor stretch loops a band around a straight leg and draws it out to the side while lying down, using the band to deepen the inner-thigh stretch. Keep the pelvis heavy on the floor and breathe into the tension; the band should pull, never yank.",
    "banded_ankle_stretch": "The banded ankle stretch anchors a band over the ankle joint and drives the knee forward over the toes, mobilizing the ankle joint as the calf lengthens. The band's posterior pull is what makes this version work where a plain lean stalls; keep the heel down throughout.",
    "banded_calf_stretch": "The banded calf stretch loops a band around the ball of the foot and pulls the toes back toward the shin with the leg straight. Keep the knee long to bias the gastrocnemius, then bend it slightly to reach the soleus; hold each version for 20 to 30 seconds.",
    "banded_chest_stretch": "The banded chest stretch holds a band wide behind the back and lifts the arms, opening the pecs and front shoulders. Walk the grip narrower to intensify or raise the arms to change the line of pull; keep the ribs down rather than arching into it.",
    "banded_clamshell": "The banded clamshell adds a band above the knees to the classic side-lying clamshell, forcing the glute medius to work against the band's pull. Keep the heels together and the pelvis still; the knee opens and nothing else moves.",
    "banded_figure_4_stretch": "The banded figure-4 stretch loops a band around one thigh and pulls the crossed ankle toward the chest while lying down, deepening the glute stretch. Keep the head and shoulders relaxed on the floor and let the band set the depth.",
    "banded_fire_hydrant": "The banded fire hydrant lifts the knee sideways from a quadruped position against a band above the knees, targeting the glute medius. Keep the hips square to the floor and the torso quiet; small, controlled arcs beat big swings.",
    "banded_glute_bridge": "The banded glute bridge bridges the hips up with a band pulling the knees inward, so the glutes must push out as well as extend. Keep the band under constant tension at the top and squeeze hard; the knees should track over the toes, never cave.",
    "banded_hamstring_stretch": "The banded hamstring stretch lies on the back with a band looped around the foot and draws the straight leg toward the chest. Keep the other leg heavy on the floor and the knee of the working leg long; the band sets the depth, not the arm strength.",
    "banded_hip_thrust": "The banded hip thrust drives the hips to extension against a band looped over the pelvis and anchored under the feet. The resistance rises exactly where the glutes are strongest, at lockout; tuck the pelvis and finish each rep with a hard squeeze.",
    "banded_it_band_stretch": "The banded IT-band stretch lies on the back with a band around the foot and draws the straight leg across the body toward the opposite shoulder. Keep the pelvis and the opposite shoulder heavy on the floor; the stretch should run down the outer thigh, not wrench the knee.",
    "banded_kneeling_hip_thrust": "The banded kneeling hip thrust kneels tall with a band over the pelvis and pushes the hips forward to full extension, training the glutes in the standing hip-extension pattern. Keep the ribs down and squeeze the glutes to finish; the band's pull rises toward lockout.",
    "banded_lat_stretch": "The banded lat stretch holds a band overhead and leans sideways, letting the band lengthen the lats along the ribs. Anchor the hips and keep both feet grounded; breathe into the stretched side and let the arm travel with the band rather than fighting it.",
    "banded_lateral_walk": "The banded lateral walk side-steps against a band around the ankles or knees, keeping constant outward tension on the glute medius. Stay low in an athletic quarter squat and never let the knees cave between steps; equal distances each way.",
    "banded_rear_delt_stretch": "The banded rear delt stretch crosses a band in front of the body and draws the arms across the chest, opening the back of the shoulders. Keep the neck relaxed and the shoulders down; a light, sustained pull does more than a hard yank.",
    "banded_romanian_deadlift": "The banded Romanian deadlift hinges under a band anchored at the feet, where resistance increases through the lockout exactly as the glutes and hamstrings finish. Keep the spine long and push the hips back; the band makes the top of the rep the hardest part.",
    "banded_seated_hip_abduction": "The banded seated hip abduction pushes the knees apart against a band while seated, isolating the upper glutes with nothing but a loop. Sit tall and keep the feet still; the knees travel and the torso does not.",
    "banded_shoulder_stretch": "The banded shoulder stretch draws a band overhead and behind the back in a slow arc, opening the shoulders through their full range. Keep the elbows long and the grip adjustable, since narrower is harder; never force past a pinching shoulder.",
    "banded_squat": "The banded squat squats against a band anchored under the feet and over the shoulders, so the load grows toward lockout where a barbell is easiest. Keep the chest tall and the knees tracking out; the band rewards full, smooth extensions.",
    "banded_standing_hip_abduction": "The banded standing hip abduction swings the leg out to the side against an ankle band, training the glute medius in a standing posture. Keep the torso upright and square, since leaning away cheats the rep; the range is small and that is fine.",
    "banded_standing_hip_adduction": "The banded standing hip adduction draws the leg across the body against a band anchored to the side, working the adductors from a standing base. Stand tall on the supporting leg and sweep slowly; the crossing leg does the work and the trunk stays quiet.",
    "banded_standing_leg_curl": "The banded standing leg curl curls the heel toward the glute against an ankle-anchored band from a standing position, isolating the hamstrings of the working leg. Keep the thigh vertical and the hips square; control the return, as the band wants to snap the leg back.",
    "banded_sumo_walk": "The banded sumo walk walks forward and backward in a wide, low stance against a band around the knees or ankles, keeping constant outward tension on the hips. Stay in the quarter squat the whole time; short, wide steps and level hips.",
    "banded_terminal_knee_extension": "The banded terminal knee extension straightens the knee against a band pulling it backward, retraining the quad's final lockout after injury or long sitting. The band sits behind the knee and the heel stays down; the movement is small, precise and important.",
    "banded_triceps_stretch": "The banded triceps stretch holds a band overhead in one hand and draws the elbow back with the other, lengthening the triceps behind the arm. Keep the ribs down and the neck long; a gentle sustained pull with slow breathing loosens the elbow's lockout range.",
    "cable_bent_over_row": "The cable bent-over row hinges forward and rows a cable attachment to the lower ribs, pulling against constant resistance through the whole range. The cable's line differs from a barbell, so the lats and mid-back work without lower-back compression; keep the torso steady and the elbows driving back.",
    "cable_chest_press": "The cable chest press presses two handles forward from the chest from a standing or seated stance. The cables pull slightly apart through the press, so the pecs stabilize as well as push; step into a staggered stance and keep the wrists stacked over the elbows.",
    "cable_curl": "The cable curl curls a handle or bar from a low pulley, keeping tension on the biceps at both the top and the bottom of every rep. Keep the elbows pinned to the sides and resist the weight on the way down; the constant load is the point.",
    "cable_external_rotation": "The cable external rotation rotates the upper arm outward against a low cable with the elbow pinned at the side, training the rotator cuff directly. Go light, since this is a precision drill rather than a strength showcase; control the return slowly.",
    "cable_fly": "The cable fly sweeps two pulley handles together in a wide arc in front of the chest, loading the pecs through constant tension. Keep a soft, fixed elbow bend and let the arms draw the arc from the shoulders; squeeze the hands together at the front for a beat.",
    "cable_glute_kickback": "The cable glute kickback extends the leg straight back against an ankle cuff from a low pulley, isolating the glute of the working hip. Keep the torso square to the machine; the temptation to arch is what the drill trains away. Squeeze the glute to finish, not the lower back.",
    "cable_lateral_raise": "The cable lateral raise raises one arm out to the side against a low pulley, loading the side delt with tension from the very first degree. Keep the elbow slightly bent and the torso still; the cable's constant pull makes lighter weights feel honest.",
    "cable_tricep_kickback": "The cable tricep kickback hinges forward and extends the forearm back against a low cable, keeping tension on the triceps through the entire arc. Pin the upper arm parallel to the floor and let only the forearm move; the cable fixes the sagging resistance of the dumbbell version.",
    "cable_tricep_pushdown": "The cable tricep pushdown extends the arms down against a high pulley, the staple triceps isolation with constant resistance. Pin the elbows to the ribs and split the hands slightly at the bottom; control the return rather than letting the stack fall.",
    "cable_upright_row": "The cable upright row pulls a bar or rope up the front of the body from a low pulley, training the side delts and upper traps. Keep the hands no wider than the shoulders and stop at chest height; the cable keeps the load smooth where a barbell jars.",
    "cable_wrist_curl": "The cable wrist curl flexes the wrists against a low cable with the forearms braced on the thighs or a bench. Constant tension makes even light weights effective; use full range and high reps for the flexors.",
    "kneeling_cable_row": "The kneeling cable row kneels facing a low pulley and rows the handle to the ribs, forcing the core to hold the torso upright without a bench or seat. Keep the hips square and the pull strong through the elbow; the kneeling stance quietly doubles as a hip-flexor stretch.",
    "one_arm_lat_pulldown": "The one-arm lat pulldown pulls a single handle down beside the body, letting each lat work through its own range without the stronger side covering. Keep the torso square and reach tall at the top; the stretch under load is the best part of the rep.",
    "single_arm_tricep_pushdown": "The single-arm tricep pushdown extends one arm down against a cable, keeping constant tension from the very top of the rep. Keep the upper arm glued to the side and squeeze fully at lockout; the free hand can steady the torso.",
    "straight_bar_cable_front_raise": "The straight-bar cable front raise raises a bar from a low pulley to shoulder height in front of the body, loading the front delts under constant tension. Keep the arms nearly straight and the torso still; resist the cable all the way down.",
    "v_bar_tricep_pushdown": "The V-bar tricep pushdown uses the angled V handle to press down against a high pulley, angling the hands naturally outward. The neutral grip spares the wrists and elbows; keep the elbows fixed and finish each rep with a full lockout.",
    "wide_grip_seated_cable_row": "The wide-grip seated cable row rows a wide bar to the upper abdomen with the elbows flared, shifting emphasis toward the rear delts and mid-back. Sit tall, pull the shoulder blades together at the finish and keep the torso from rocking with the weight.",
}
